Stores the real-time quantity on hand of a product (and lot/serial) in a specific location. It is the single source of truth for current inventory levels in Odoo.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Display stock availability (on hand, reserved, available)
Support real-time inventory in Sales, Purchase, Manufacturing, and POS
Enable stock valuation and accounting entries
Basis for reservation, replenishment, and MRP
Inventory adjustments and cycle counts
Lot/serial number traceability and aging
Multi-warehouse and multi-location stock overview

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent, high-performance)
Key Fields:
product_id → product.product (required)
location_id → stock.location (required)
lot_id → stock.lot (optional)
quantity (float), reserved_quantity (float)
inventory_quantity (for adjustments), inventory_date
owner_id, package_id, company_id
Computed: available_quantity (= quantity - reserved_quantity)

Critical Hooks: _update_available_quantity, _gather, action_apply_inventory, create / write (strict concurrency control)
Security: stock.group_stock_manager + strict location/company rules (very protected)

RAG Routing Keywords:
stock quant, quantity on hand, stock level, inventory quantity, available stock, reserved quantity, on hand qty, stock.quant, real-time stock, lot quantity, location stock, current inventory
Related Models (most joined):

product.product
stock.location
stock.lot
stock.move / stock.move.line (updates quants)
stock.picking
stock.valuation.layer (for costing)

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
stock.quant is Odoo’s core real-time inventory model that holds current quantity and reserved_quantity of a product_id in a specific location_id (and lot_id). It is automatically updated by every stock.move, serves as the single source of truth for stock availability, reservations, valuation, and is heavily queried by Sales, Manufacturing, POS, and reporting across the entire system.